# Trimmed to what the build context actually needs. Nothing here changes
# which files land in the image -- the Dockerfile's COPY lines already name
# those explicitly -- this only stops an unused .pbix sample or a checked-out
# .git history from being sent to the Docker daemon on every build.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/dist-embedded
frontend/node_modules
data/models/*.pbix
# The three the Dockerfile actually COPYs back in -- StoreSales is the model
# the deployment opens on, and the mismatch here (this file excluded every
# .pbix with no exceptions, while the Dockerfile only ever copied the TMDL
# folders) is exactly why a deployed container was silently serving
# ClinicalTrialSafety instead of StoreSales: the file simply never reached the
# build context, so `start.sh`'s own "if [ -e "$model" ]" check saw nothing
# there and skipped it without failing the build.
!data/models/StoreSales.pbix
!data/models/Supply_Chain_Sample.pbix
!data/models/Sales_Returns_Sample.pbix
data/samples
tests
docs
*.md
!README.md
